-- Presentation intent: how a structure should be drawn, in the closed vocabulary of
-- src/shared/presentation.ts. Lanes, order, roles, emphasis, folds and direction. No coordinate,
-- no colour, no CSS — those are layer 3 and are worked out by ELK on every draw.
--
-- Generated by drizzle-kit from src/server/db/schema.ts, then edited BY HAND to add
-- `IF NOT EXISTS`, exactly as 0001 was. Read both notes before changing anything here.
--
-- WHY `IF NOT EXISTS` IS ADDED BY HAND, EVERY TIME.
-- drizzle-kit emits a bare `CREATE TABLE`. Three tables in a real PanelX database are created
-- outside the migration system, by `ensureLayoutTable()` in api/layout.ts and
-- `ensureSourceIndexTables()` in lib/sourceindex.ts, which run `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` at
-- import. A bare `CREATE TABLE` in a migration fails against every database one of those has
-- already touched, with `table … already exists`, out of a command whose whole job is to be run
-- again. `presentation_intent` has no `ensure*` function and must never grow one — this migration
-- is where it is created, and two definitions of one table is this codebase's recurring defect
-- written in SQL, failing at runtime on INSERT rather than at compile time.
--
-- WHAT MAKES IT SAFE TO RUN TWICE, AND SAFE AGAINST A DATABASE WITH REAL ROWS IN IT.
-- drizzle writes a row into `__drizzle_migrations` carrying this migration's `when` value from
-- drizzle/meta/_journal.json, and afterwards applies only files whose `when` is later than the
-- newest row there. src/server/db/migrate.ts checks that journal exists before running anything.
--
-- NOTHING BELOW TOUCHES AN EXISTING ROW. One new table is created and no other table is read,
-- rewritten, rebuilt or altered. Every record, link and change keeps every value it had; a
-- database that has never had presentation intent written to it simply gains an empty table.
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS `presentation_intent` (
	`workspace_id` text DEFAULT 'default' NOT NULL,
	`scope` text NOT NULL,
	`target` text NOT NULL,
	`intent` text NOT NULL,
	`updated_at` text NOT NULL,
	`updated_by` text NOT NULL,
	PRIMARY KEY(`workspace_id`, `scope`, `target`)
);
